"use strict";(self.webpackChunkquickbooks_connector_doc=self.webpackChunkquickbooks_connector_doc||[]).push([[102],{1002(e,t,a){a.r(t),a.d(t,{comp:()=>l,data:()=>i});var o=a(641);const n={},l=(0,a(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,o.uX)(),(0,o.CE)("div",null,[t[0]||(t[0]=(0,o.Fv)("<h1 id=\"sync-monitor\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#sync-monitor\"><span>Sync Monitor</span></a></h1><p>The <strong>Sync Monitor</strong> is your operational control center in WooCommerce QuickBooks Connector. Introduced in <strong>v4.0.0</strong>, it replaces disparate legacy log tables with a unified monitoring suite featuring real-time sync KPIs, activity timelines, detailed JSON payload inspectors, and one-click failure retries.</p><p>Open <strong>Webkul WC Addons \u2192 WC Quick Book Connector \u2192 Sync Monitor</strong>.</p><p><img src=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/images/quickbooks-connector/sync-monitor.webp\" alt=\"Sync Monitor overview showing 7-day sync activity, success rates, and store records not yet in QuickBooks\"></p><hr><h2 id=\"monitor-architecture\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#monitor-architecture\"><span>Monitor Architecture &amp; Sub-Tabs</span></a></h2><p>The Sync Monitor consolidates sync administration into three specialized sub-tabs:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Sub-Tab</th><th>Purpose &amp; Capabilities</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Overview</strong></td><td>Visual sync health KPIs, 7/14/30-day activity trends, and real-time reconciliation queues of store records not yet exported to QuickBooks.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Activity</strong></td><td>Granular event-by-event sync logs for every entity with detailed payload inspectors, error messages, and one-click manual retry buttons.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Logs</strong></td><td>Direct access to WooCommerce system logs (<code>wc-quickbook-errors</code>, <code>wc-quickbook-sync</code>) with severity filters, log download, and purge options.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"overview-subtab\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#overview-subtab\"><span>1. Overview Sub-Tab</span></a></h2><p>The Overview tab presents high-level synchronization health at a glance:</p><ul><li><strong>KPI Metric Cards</strong> \u2014 displays <strong>Total Records Synced</strong>, overall <strong>Success Rate (%)</strong>, <strong>Pending Queue Items</strong>, and <strong>Failed Records</strong>.</li><li><strong>Sync Activity Chart</strong> \u2014 toggle between <strong>7 Days</strong>, <strong>14 Days</strong>, and <strong>30 Days</strong> to observe sync execution volumes and success-to-failure ratios over time.</li><li><strong>Store Records Not in QuickBooks Yet</strong> \u2014 dynamic reconciliation panels that list:<ul><li><strong>Unsynced Products</strong> \u2014 WooCommerce catalog items pending initial export or modification sync.</li><li><strong>Unsynced Orders</strong> \u2014 customer purchases ready for export with status pills and totals.</li><li><strong>Unsynced Customers</strong> \u2014 registered buyers not yet matched to QuickBooks customer profiles.</li></ul>Each record row includes an inline <strong>Export / Sync Now</strong> button to immediately sync the item to QuickBooks without switching screens.</li></ul><h2 id=\"activity-subtab\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#activity-subtab\"><span>2. Activity Sub-Tab</span></a></h2><p>The Activity sub-tab provides a comprehensive audit trail of every synchronization transaction:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Entity Type</strong></td><td>Customer, Product, Order, Payment, Refund Receipt, Deposit, or Journal Entry</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Record ID / SKU</strong></td><td>WooCommerce record identifier, order number, or product SKU</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Direction</strong></td><td><strong>WooCommerce \u2192 QuickBooks</strong> (Export) or <strong>QuickBooks \u2192 WooCommerce</strong> (Import/Webhook)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Trigger Source</strong></td><td><strong>Auto Sync</strong> (event trigger), <strong>Webhook</strong> (real-time IPN), or <strong>Manual Export</strong> (admin bulk action)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Status</strong></td><td>Green <strong>Success</strong> badge or red <strong>Failed</strong> badge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Message / Error</strong></td><td>Detailed message returned by the synchronization engine or Intuit API error code (e.g. <code>Error 6240: Duplicate Name</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Actions</strong></td><td><strong>View Details</strong> (modal popup with raw JSON) and <strong>Retry</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"hint-container tip\"><p class=\"hint-container-title\">Payload &amp; Response Inspector</p><p>Clicking <strong>View Details</strong> opens an interactive inspector showing the exact request JSON dispatched to QuickBooks and Intuit&#39;s raw response. This makes troubleshooting schema mismatches, missing accounts, or tax validation issues straightforward.</p></div><h3 id=\"retrying-failed-items\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#retrying-failed-items\"><span>One-Click Retries</span></a></h3><ol><li>Locate any failed row in the Activity table (marked with a red <strong>Failed</strong> badge).</li><li>Click the <strong>Retry</strong> button on the row.</li><li>The sync engine immediately re-queues the record and attempts re-synchronization with QuickBooks Online.</li><li>You can also select multiple failed rows and execute <strong>Bulk Retry</strong> from the bulk actions dropdown.</li></ol><h2 id=\"logs-subtab\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#logs-subtab\"><span>3. Logs Sub-Tab</span></a></h2><p>The Logs sub-tab connects directly to the underlying WooCommerce logging system located under <code>wp-content/uploads/wc-logs/</code>:</p><ul><li><strong>Log Selection</strong> \u2014 view live entries from <code>wc-quickbook-errors</code> or <code>wc-quickbook-sync</code>.</li><li><strong>Severity Filtering</strong> \u2014 filter entries by severity level: <strong>All</strong>, <strong>Critical / Error</strong>, <strong>Warning</strong>, <strong>Info</strong>, or <strong>Debug</strong>.</li><li><strong>Download Log File</strong> \u2014 export the entire raw log as a text file for Webkul support tickets or offline audit.</li><li><strong>Clear / Purge Log</strong> \u2014 delete obsolete log entries to reclaim disk space.</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"action-scheduler-engine\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#action-scheduler-engine\"><span>Action Scheduler Background Engine</span></a></h2><p>All background synchronization tasks, webhook event processing, and bulk queue batches are powered by <strong>WooCommerce Action Scheduler</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>No WP-Cron Dependency</strong> \u2014 sync jobs do not rely on storefront traffic and execute reliably via server crons or runner threads.</li><li><strong>Automatic 3x Exponential Retries</strong> \u2014 temporary network drops or Intuit rate-limiting (HTTP 429) automatically reschedule with backoff intervals.</li><li><strong>Concurrency Safety</strong> \u2014 token refresh mutex locks prevent race conditions during high-volume parallel order exports.</li></ul><div class=\"hint-container tip\"><p class=\"hint-container-title\">Automated Failure Email Alerts</p><p>Rather than checking the Sync Monitor manually, enable <strong>Email Notifications</strong> in <a class=\"route-link\" href=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/quickbooks-connector/general-settings.html\">General Settings</a> to automatically receive digest reports and immediate failure alerts delivered to your administrative email address.</p></div><hr><h2 id=\"related-features\" tabindex=\"-1\"><a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#related-features\"><span>Related Features</span></a></h2><ul><li><a class=\"route-link\" href=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/quickbooks-connector/auto-sync.html\">Auto Sync Settings</a> \u2014 configure background triggers and 2-way stock sync</li><li><a class=\"route-link\" href=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/quickbooks-connector/export-order-settings.html\">Export Order Settings</a> \u2014 transaction types, fee mappings, and rounding adjustments</li><li><a class=\"route-link\" href=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/quickbooks-connector/orders.html\">Orders</a> \u2014 manual export controls and WooCommerce orders sync column</li><li><a class=\"route-link\" href=\"/woocommerce-quickbooks-connector/quickbooks-connector/changelog.html\">Changelog</a> \u2014 full release history of new features and fixes</li></ul>",28))])}]]);var i={"path":"/quickbooks-connector/sync-monitor.html","title":"Sync Monitor","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Sync Monitor","description":"Sync health and audit logs"},"headers":[]}}}]);